---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { person } from '../data/site.js';

// Every statement here describes what this site actually does today. Nothing
// about retention periods, processors or the controller's contact details is
// invented — where an answer is missing the page routes the reader to the
// contact page rather than stating a policy nobody has agreed to.
const formLive = Boolean(person.formEndpoint);
---

<Base
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="How this website handles personal data, what it collects, and what it does not."
>
  <PageHeader
    title="Privacy notice"
    standfirst="What this website collects, why, and what it does not do."
  />

  <section class="field-light pad">
    <div class="wrap doc prose">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets no cookies, runs no analytics, and shows no advertising. It does not track
        you between visits or across other websites. The only personal data it can receive is what
        you type into the enquiry form and send deliberately.
      </p>

      <h2>The enquiry form</h2>
      {
        formLive ? (
          <p>
            The form collects your name, email address, the subject you select, your message, and
            your organisation if you choose to give it. These are used to reply to you and for
            nothing else. They are not sold, published, or used for any mailing list.
          </p>
        ) : (
          <p>
            The enquiry form is not connected to any service yet, so it currently collects and
            transmits nothing at all. When it is connected it will collect your name, email address,
            the subject you select, your message, and your organisation if you choose to give it —
            used to reply to you and for nothing else, never sold, published, or added to a mailing
            list.
          </p>
        )
      }
      <p>
        The consent checkbox on the form is there because sending an enquiry means handing over
        personal data, and that should be a deliberate act rather than a side effect.
      </p>

      <h2>Fonts are loaded from Google</h2>
      <p>
        The typefaces used here are served by Google Fonts. Your browser requests them from
        <code>fonts.googleapis.com</code> and <code>fonts.gstatic.com</code>, which means your IP
        address and basic browser information reach Google when a page loads. No cookie is set by
        this, and it is the only third party the site contacts. It can be removed entirely by
        serving the font files from this domain instead.
      </p>

      <h2>Server logs</h2>
      <p>
        Like any website, the server that delivers these pages keeps standard access logs. What is
        recorded and for how long is determined by the hosting provider rather than by this site.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act gives you the right to ask what personal data
        is held about you, to have it corrected, and to have it erased. If you have sent an enquiry
        and want it deleted, say so and it will be deleted.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a class="link" href="/contact/">Get in touch</a> about anything on this page.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this notice changes, the revised version replaces this one on this page. There is no
        mailing list to notify, because there is no mailing list.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .doc {
    font-size: var(--t-base);
  }
  .doc h2 {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-variation-settings: 'wdth' 90;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: var(--t-md);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-top: var(--s-7);
    padding-top: var(--s-4);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .doc h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
    padding-top: 0;
    border-top: 0;
  }
  .doc code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 0.9em;
    color: var(--text);
  }
</style>
